{"kind":"pair","a":"R0014","b":"R0003","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Shared authors (Yuben Qu, Chao Dong, Lei Zhang, Qihui Wu) and shared NSFC grants 61931011 and 62072303","reason":"No version claim or cross-citation; distinct systems and problems under P07: R0014 proposes ASAP for hierarchical inter-cluster model partitioning and intra-cluster data partitioning with elastic scheduling, whereas R0003 proposes DMS for dynamic switching between large and small DNN models.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0014.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"ASAP respectively partitions DL model and data among UAV clusters and within each cluster, and two-layer load balancing and elastic scheduling algorithms are designed to perform efficient and robust collaborative computing."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0003.pdf","page":1,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"In this paper, we investigate how to achieve high-accuracy and low-latency edge intelligence in a UAV swarm, by dynamically switching between large complex and small lightweight DNN models."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0014","b":"R0010","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Shared authors (Yuben Qu, Chao Dong, Lei Zhang, Qihui Wu) and shared NSFC grants 61931011 and 62072303","reason":"No version claim or cross-citation; distinct architectures and algorithms under P07: R0014 partitions models across clusters and data within clusters in ASAP, whereas R0010 treats each UAV as a sequential pipeline stage for linear chain collaborative inference.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0014.pdf","page":4,"section":"III. SYSTEM OVERVIEW","quote":"First, the complete DL model is partitioned into three submodels for each cluster"},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0010.pdf","page":2,"section":"III.A System Model","quote":"The system consists of N UAVs, and each UAV is a stage of the pipeline."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0014","b":"R0015","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Shared authors (Hao Sun, Yuben Qu, Chao Dong, Lei Zhang, Qihui Wu) and shared NSFC grants 61931011 and 62072303","reason":"No version claim or cross-citation; distinct formulations and execution designs under P07: R0014 builds ASAP with hierarchical cluster model and data partitioning plus latency prediction and compression, whereas R0015 proposes the online heuristic EECIA for energy-efficient task allocation.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0014.pdf","page":5,"section":"III. SYSTEM OVERVIEW","quote":"the proposed architecture partitions the DL model and data among UAV clusters and within each cluster, respectively, which avoids data relay in the swarm"},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0015.pdf","page":5,"section":"III.C Online Heuristic","quote":"Therefore, we propose an online heuristic solution called EECIA to perform the real-time allocation, as shown in Algorithm 1."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0014","b":"R0059","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Shared authors (Yuben Qu, Chao Dong, Lei Zhang, Qihui Wu) and shared NSFC grant 61931011","reason":"No version claim or cross-citation; distinct investigations under P07: R0014 designs ASAP with an elastic scheduler, DNN block predictor, and data compressor for swarm inference, whereas R0059 designs AMSM for adaptive model switching and partitioning across multi-CNN streams.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0014.pdf","page":4,"section":"III. SYSTEM OVERVIEW","quote":"the system is composed of three modules, i.e., elastic efficient task scheduler (Section IV), lightweight accurate DNN block performance predictor (Section V), and adaptive inter-UAV inference data compressor (Section VI)."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0059.pdf","page":2,"section":"1. Introduction","quote":"To solve this problem, we propose an efficient algorithm called Adaptive Model Switching of collaborative inference for Multi-CNN streams (AMSM) that can determine the strategy for model switching and model partitioning with a low latency."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0014","b":"R0062","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Shared authors (Hao Sun, Yuben Qu, Chao Dong, Haipeng Dai, Qihui Wu, Song Guo) and shared NSFC grants 61931011 and 62072303; both evaluate UAV swarm collaborative inference with Jetson prototypes","reason":"No explicit version linkage or shared underlying investigation under P07: R0014 is a full research study introducing ASAP (cluster model/data partitioning, E2S scheduler, operator predictor, adaptive compressor on a 24-Jetson and 5-UAV testbed), whereas R0062 is a magazine architecture article introducing the OODA-loop eCoEI framework with a separate four-UAV prototype.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0014.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"In this paper, we propose a novel system named ASAP (All-Sky Autonomous comPuting) that could fast and accurately process the UAV sensory data, solely by the autonomous collaboration within the UAV swarm"},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0062.pdf","page":2,"section":"INTRODUCTION","quote":"This article proposes the eCoEI (elastic collaborative edge intelligence) for UAV swarm networks, a brand new architecture based on OODA (i.e., Observation, Orientation, Decision and Action) loop"}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0036","b":"R0048","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Both study multi-UAV video analytics in 2026 IEEE Transactions with superficial author-name similarity (Wen Wu vs Wenbo Wu)","reason":"Disjoint authors, affiliations, funding, and system designs with no version claim or cross-citation: R0036 optimizes edge-assisted UAV selection, frame rate, and resolution via scene-adaptive profiling and k-swap local search, whereas R0048 proposes UCAA with centralized and distributed control modes for collaborative video analytics.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0036.pdf","page":5,"section":"III.A System Model","quote":"We focus on the joint UAV selection and configuration control problem in an edge-assisted low-altitude surveillance video analytics system, which requires the edge server to schedule the UAVs for video chunk uploading while controlling the frame rate/resolution of the video appropriately."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0048.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"We develop an adaptive multi-UAV collaborative video analytics architecture (UCAA), which incorporates both centralized and distributed control modes."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0075","b":"R0080","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Both study confidence-based collaborative DNN inference for multi-UAV networks evaluated on CIFAR-10","reason":"Disjoint author teams, institutions, grants, and frameworks with no version claim or cross-citation: R0075 proposes CIDER combining offline channel-partitioned early-exit distillation with online contextual bandit routing across UAVs, whereas R0080 proposes an air-ground edge-cloud model collaboration framework optimizing confidence thresholds and quantization bits for non-IID data.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0075.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"Motivated by this, we propose CIDER, which consists of an offline channel-partitioning distillation stage and an online context-aware routing stage."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0080.pdf","page":1,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"To address this, we propose an air-ground model collaboration framework with non-identically distributed sensory data."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0110","b":"R0074","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Both study distributed LLM inference in UAV swarms and R0110 explicitly cites R0074 (Orion) as reference [39] and evaluates an Orion-based baseline","reason":"Disjoint author teams, institutions, and grants; R0110 treats R0074 (Orion) as distinct prior work and proposes RDI-LLM with affinity-aware redundant FFN shard placement and resilient first-successful aggregation, whereas R0074 proposes Orion for sensor-aware edge LLM collaborative inference.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0110.pdf","page":2,"section":"II.A Distributed Transformer and LLM Inference","quote":"Among the most recent 2025-2026 systems, Orion [39] optimizes prefill-oriented pipeline execution over heterogeneous UAV-edge nodes through dynamic-programming model partitioning and adaptive sequence partitioning"},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0074.pdf","page":3,"section":"1. Introduction","quote":"Motivated by these gaps, we propose Orion, a novel collaborative inference framework for sensor-aware LLM deployment at the edge."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0118","b":"R0083","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Shared authors (HyungBin Park, SuKyoung Lee at Yonsei University) and shared NRF grant 2022R1A2B5B01001683, both studying distributed DNN inference in UAV swarms","reason":"No version claim or cross-citation; distinct architectures and optimization problems under P07: R0118 proposes NetMoE integrating mixture-of-experts distributed inference with joint trajectory planning, whereas R0083 proposes a battery- and compute-aware DNN deployment method minimizing end-to-end latency and energy usage.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0118.pdf","page":1,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"To address these open challenges, we propose NetMoE, a framework that integrates MoE-based distributed inference with joint trajectory planning on a UAV swarm."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0083.pdf","page":2,"section":"1. Introduction","quote":"We propose a deployment method that is aware of a varying set of DNN models and UAVs in terms of computational and battery capacity and deploys the models to minimizing e2e latency and energy usage."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0137","b":"R0045","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Both study reinforcement-learning-based DNN inference in multi-UAV-assisted MEC systems in 2026 IEEE journals","reason":"Disjoint authors, affiliations, grants, and system models with no version claim or cross-citation: R0137 proposes RUVA using Dec-POMDP MARL with Poisson reliability modeling for video analytics offloading, resolution, and model selection, whereas R0045 proposes SAC-PER with a convex optimization subroutine for layer-wise DNN partitioning, 3D trajectory, and inter-UAV task migration.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0137.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"In this paper, we focus on the problem of reliability-aware video analytics services in UAV-assisted MEC network."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0045.pdf","page":3,"section":"I.B Contributions and Organization","quote":"Specifically, we propose a soft actor-critic with prioritized experience replay (SAC-PER) algorithm and incorporate a CO-based UAV computing resource allocation subproblem solver for each time slot."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0106","b":"R0054","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Both investigate multi-UAV ISCC networks with collaborative DNN splitting and multi-agent deep reinforcement learning","reason":"Disjoint authors, institutions, grants, and system formulations with no version claim or cross-citation: R0106 addresses fault-tolerant group target sensing with disabled UAVs via split learning and masked MA-DDPG, whereas R0054 develops a hierarchical semantic-aware framework for heading-coupled STAR-RIS assisted multi-UAV ISCC networks.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0106.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"we allow the rest of the working UAVs (W-UAVs) to collaboratively complete the inference task of the D-UAVs based on the split learning (SL) to improve the robustness of the GTST."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0054.pdf","page":1,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"We address this gap by developing a hierarchical semantic-aware framework for heading-coupled STAR-RIS assisted multi-UAV ISCC networks."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0092","b":"R0001","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Additional credible candidate: shared authors (Songwei Li, Jiebei Shi, Jiwei Huang at China University of Petroleum, Beijing) and shared grants (NSFC 62572484 and CUP 2462024XKQY003)","reason":"No version claim or cross-citation; distinct architectures, algorithms, and problem settings under P07: R0092 proposes DDCI for infrastructure-free decentralized UAV-to-UAV collaborative inference with Pareto Top-K neighbor selection, DQN partitioning, and MiniBatch pipelining, whereas R0001 proposes CAPRI for three-tier cloud-edge-end collaborative inference using PPO and analytical convex optimization.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0092.pdf","page":1,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"Motivated by the above analysis, we propose DDCI (DRL-assisted Decentralized Collaborative Inference), a framework for intelligent collaborative DNN inference in UAV swarms."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0001.pdf","page":1,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"We formulate a latency-energy coupled optimization problem for multi-UAV inference services and propose a Cloud-Edge-End Adaptive Partitioning and Resource Allocation method for Collaborative Inference(CAPRI)."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0014","b":"R0006","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Additional credible candidate: shared author (Yuben Qu at Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics) and both study UAV swarm collaborative DNN inference","reason":"No version claim or cross-citation and disjoint funding; distinct problems and methodologies under P07: R0014 proposes ASAP for autonomous cluster-based model and data partitioning with elastic scheduling and compression, whereas R0006 proposes AirInfer for joint UAV spatial deployment and sequential model partitioning under area-coverage constraints via DP and SCA.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0014.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"ASAP respectively partitions DL model and data among UAV clusters and within each cluster, and two-layer load balancing and elastic scheduling algorithms are designed to perform efficient and robust collaborative computing."},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0006.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"To address the aforementioned challenges, we propose AirInfer, a novel collaborative UAV inference framework that minimizes end-to-end inference latency through joint optimization of model partitioning and UAV deployment, subject to stringent resource and coverage constraints."}}
{"kind":"pair","a":"R0014","b":"R0009","decision":"DISTINCT","signal":"Additional credible candidate: shared author (Chao Dong at Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics) and both study multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference","reason":"No version claim or cross-citation and disjoint funding; distinct system roles and algorithms under P07: R0014 executes autonomous in-swarm collaborative inference across UAV clusters in ASAP, whereas R0009 offloads ground-user DNN tasks to MEC UAVs via DPDTS combining OPPS, fairness matching, and TD3 trajectory optimization.","evidence_a":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0014.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"In this paper, we propose a novel system named ASAP (All-Sky Autonomous comPuting) that could fast and accurately process the UAV sensory data, solely by the autonomous collaboration within the UAV swarm"},"evidence_b":{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0009.pdf","page":2,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"To further reduce system overhead, we propose a DRL-based DNN Partitioning and Dynamic Trajectory Selection (DPDTS) algorithm."}}
